# --- MANTIS data ----------------------------------------------------------
# Generated populations are reproducible from a seed; do not commit them.
data/generated/*
!data/generated/.gitkeep

# ...except the arena result. arena.json is the Day 5 gate artefact -- the evasion
# curve and the zero-day comparison -- and it is committed for exactly the reason
# the LLM cache is: a judge cloning this repo should be able to read the curve
# without spending thirty-five minutes regenerating it. It is a few kilobytes of
# JSON, it is reproducible from `python -m mantis.loop` with the default seed, and
# RESULTS.md is rendered from it.
!data/generated/arena.json

# ...and the three small artefacts the live console and the submission document
# are served from. Same reasoning as arena.json and as the LLM cache: HARD RULE 4
# says the repo must run from a clean clone with no GPU and no network, and the
# console is on the "never cut" list. A judge who clones this and runs
# `make api` must get a working authorisation stream without first spending two
# minutes fitting LightGBM.
#
# console_feed.json is ~1 MB of pre-scored authorisations and is the only one of
# these that is not trivially small; it is committed anyway, because without it
# the demo does not exist. Regenerate any of them with `make feed` / `make ood`.
# The parquets above it stay ignored - they are 15-85 MB and reproducible.
!data/generated/console_feed.json
!data/generated/l3_ood.json
!data/generated/population.manifest.json
!data/generated/dataset_v1.manifest.json

# The LLM cache IS committed on purpose. A judge cloning this repo will not
# have Ollama running, so the cache is what makes `make demo` work offline.
# See CLAUDE.md HARD RULE 3. Do not add data/cache/ here.

# Model artefacts are rebuilt by the pipeline.
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.lgb

# Never commit credentials. The repo must not need any.
.env
*.pem
kaggle.json
